{
  "rule": "nn_diffusion_mpas",
  "metric": "Linf",
  "expected_min_order": 1.0,
  "notes": "dv/dc-weighted nearest-neighbor diffusion on a quasi-uniform MPAS Voronoi mesh. The formula uses coeff = dv_edge / (dc_edge * area_cell). Asymptotic L-inf convergence is first-order rather than second-order because cells adjacent to the geographic north pole (which falls at the center of a hexagonal Voronoi cell, not at an icosahedral vertex) have u = sin(lon)*cos(lat) -> 0, so the true Laplacian is O(h) while the formula truncation error is of the same order, giving constant ~7% relative error and O(h) absolute L-inf error. L2 convergence is approximately 1.5 order (edge-band cells on icosahedral great-circle arcs dominate). Over the x1.642 -> x1.2562 -> x1.10242 sequence the observed L-inf orders are approximately [1.15, 1.06]; we require min order >= 1.0."
}